+## Review where an opt-out came from
+
+Use the web dashboard for this task, including in your phone’s browser.
+
+Select a business number to see requests received on that line. For a keyword opt-out, choose **View message**. Where AI review is available, the AI-detected entry shows its excerpt and time directly. A number filter identifies where the original request arrived. It does not limit the protection to that number.
+
+A whole-message **STOP** works separately from AI recognition. Recognition of everyday requests such as “Please don’t contact me again” is off by default. There is no customer switch for recognition. When Nixflex makes it available, it applies to eligible incoming texts with automatic SMS replies enabled. A recognised request blocks future calls and texts on the account. The person may receive one brief goodbye in their language. A greeting, a quotation or “stop the music” does not by itself request an opt-out.
+
+If review is available, the Owner can choose **Correct AI mistake** on an eligible AI-detected entry, read the evidence and enter a reason. A keyword STOP or another independent restriction stays locked. Correcting an AI mistake does not establish permission to contact the person.
+
